Resume: plan four jobs as a checklist, do two, then finish the rest from a
new session that knows only what the checklist kept.

-- project/README.md --
# demo

A small demo repository.
-- prompt --
In this repo we need four things: (1) a LICENSE file with the MIT license for "Demo Authors", (2) a .gitignore for Go projects, (3) a Makefile with a `test` target that runs `go test ./...`, and (4) a CONTRIBUTING.md with three short rules. Set this up as a checklist, then do only items 1 and 2 now; we will continue later, in another session.
-- prompt-new --
Continue the work from before on this repo: finish whatever is left.
-- check --
after 1 file LICENSE exists
after 1 file Makefile absent
file LICENSE contains MIT
file .gitignore exists
file Makefile contains go test
file CONTRIBUTING.md exists
turn 2 tool gnovm_run >= 1
vm-persist >= 1
